Patch: ugglite ztsmsd — safe SMS dedupe, stuck-receiving report, log before
dedupe key, single-instance lock. Target: devices/xiaomi-ugglite/phone-ui/ztsmsd
in this repository, which is byte-identical to the installed daemon.

Base: sha256 b2786ed651973542c51f4cb7d828d6647d5e10ee060a2a26e047ffc550d46da8
(the installed script, copied verbatim above).
Result: sha256 c8a704b45afcfeaa8a0eaea86ea6ac0e6222f17fb50091bbfaf2d5314db3caea.

Apply from the repository root with GNU patch (the header above is skipped):

    patch -p1 < devices/xiaomi-ugglite/phone-ui/ztsmsd-dedupe-v2.patch

Effect, all additive: the dedupe key keeps the message text (dropping it loses
the second of two different messages delivered in the same second, because the
ModemManager timestamp has one-second resolution), and the legacy empty-text key
is matched and upgraded instead; the log line is written before the dedupe key;
a stuck `(receiving)` multipart object is reported once to the journal and to a
state file and is never deleted; the single-instance lock no longer kills the
daemon when the lock file cannot be opened; `/SMS/1` no longer matches
`/SMS/10`; an existing log file is not touched at startup.

Status: candidate, host-verified, not installed. 28 of 28 behavioural scenarios
pass on a fake ModemManager, including the two-messages-in-one-second case, a
poisoned empty-text key with placeholder text, a failed log append and a stuck
multipart object. The verification harness is not published (MAP.md). An earlier
draft that removed the text from the dedupe key could silently lose a message and
is not published.

Original work for this device, GPL-3.0-or-later; no upstream text copied.
Body byte-identical to the local candidate patch, which is not part of this
repository.
--- a/devices/xiaomi-ugglite/phone-ui/ztsmsd
+++ b/devices/xiaomi-ugglite/phone-ui/ztsmsd
@@ -14,6 +14,22 @@
 # ztMETRO banner ("notify") on the shell's control pipe; if that pipe is not
 # there, notify-send is tried instead.  An RSCHS/112/emergency message is
 # prefixed as urgent, wakes the screen and plays the ringtone once.
+#
+# 2026-11-15 (sms-receive task, v2) changes vs b2786ed6, all additive:
+#   1. dedupe key stays "timestamp|number|text": the text is what tells two
+#      separate SMS from one sender delivered in the same second apart, so
+#      dropping it could silently lose the second one.  The real defect was a
+#      transient EMPTY text writing "timestamp|number|" into `seen`; that key
+#      then no longer matched the later readable text and the stored SMS was
+#      re-logged.  Fixed by also matching that legacy empty-text key whenever
+#      the text is present, and by upgrading it to the full key.
+#   2. a stuck `(receiving)` SMS (incomplete multipart, e.g. SMS/1 since
+#      2026-11-05) is detected and reported ONCE to the journal and to
+#      $STATE_DIR/receiving-stale.log.  It is never deleted here; deletion is
+#      a user decision (`mmcli -s N --delete`).
+#   3. the log line is written before the dedupe key, so a failed log append
+#      no longer loses the message (it is retried next poll).
+#   4. optional single-instance flock (manual run cannot double-log).
 set -u
 
 CONF=/etc/ztsmsd.conf
@@ -29,12 +45,20 @@
 : "${SLEEP:=2}"
 : "${RING_USER:=alarm}"
 : "${ALERT_TONE:=/usr/local/share/sounds/ztos/phone/Nokia-Tune.wav}"
+# A `(received)`-less SMS object older than this is reported as stuck.
+: "${RECEIVING_STALE_SECS:=1800}"
 
 RUN_DIR=$STATE_DIR
 SEEN="$RUN_DIR/seen"
+RECEIVING="$RUN_DIR/receiving"
+WARNED="$RUN_DIR/receiving-warned"
+STUCK_LOG="$RUN_DIR/receiving-stale.log"
 mkdir -p "$RUN_DIR" "$(dirname "$SMS_LOG")" 2>/dev/null
 chmod 755 "$RUN_DIR" 2>/dev/null
-touch "$SMS_LOG" 2>/dev/null; chmod 644 "$SMS_LOG" 2>/dev/null
+# Do not `touch` an existing SMS_LOG: that rewrites its mtime and hides when the
+# last message was really appended.
+[ -e "$SMS_LOG" ] || : > "$SMS_LOG" 2>/dev/null
+chmod 644 "$SMS_LOG" 2>/dev/null
 
 RING_UID=$(id -u "$RING_USER" 2>/dev/null || echo 1000)
 : "${RING_RUNTIME:=/run/user/$RING_UID}"
@@ -43,6 +67,14 @@
 	printf '%s ztsmsd: %s\n' "$(date '+%H:%M:%S')" "$*"
 }
 
+# One instance only: a manual run must not duplicate log lines.
+if command -v flock >/dev/null 2>&1 && exec 9>"$RUN_DIR/lock" 2>/dev/null; then
+	if ! flock -n 9 2>/dev/null; then
+		log "another ztsmsd instance holds $RUN_DIR/lock; exiting"
+		exit 0
+	fi
+fi
+
